`bench call` (#612, FJ8a) is planned and refused as `call` is, before a
session opens, and refused once more when the operation is not declared
`idempotent`: a benchmark repeats a call, and repeating a write is a
different act from measuring it.

A fan-out to an operation that forbids one is refused before anything is
sent (spec §5.1 O2), and nothing moves that.

```console
$ zenctl bench call '*/tc' tc.netif.v1 'interfaces/{ns}/{iface}/set' --contracts ../examples/zk2/tcgui/tc.netif.v1.toml
? 2
Error: tc.netif.v1 @op/interfaces/{ns}/{iface}/set: declares fanout = "forbidden", and this call is a fan-out: the address */tc has a `*`. Call one address with every parameter given (spec §5.1 O2); nothing was sent

```

A concrete call to a write is refused until `--i-know` says it is meant —
here it then goes on to its session, the dead-bus fixture, whose 2 is the
session's.

```console
$ zenctl bench call host-a/tc tc.netif.v1 'interfaces/{ns}/{iface}/set' --param ns=default --param iface=eth0 '{"operation": "Enable"}' --contracts ../examples/zk2/tcgui/tc.netif.v1.toml
? 2
Error: tc.netif.v1 @op/interfaces/{ns}/{iface}/set: is not idempotent, and a benchmark calls it again and again: that is a repeated write into a live deployment, not a measurement (O4). Pass --i-know to mean it

$ zenctl bench call host-a/tc tc.netif.v1 'interfaces/{ns}/{iface}/set' --param ns=default --param iface=eth0 '{"operation": "Enable"}' --contracts ../examples/zk2/tcgui/tc.netif.v1.toml --i-know --zenoh-config tests/cmd/fixtures/dead-bus.json5
? 2
Error: failed to open the Zenoh session

Caused by:
    Unable to connect to any of [Single(tcp/127.0.0.1:1)]!

$ zenctl bench call host-a/tc tc.netif.v1 diagnostics --calls 0 --contracts ../examples/zk2/tcgui/tc.netif.v1.toml
? 2
Error: --calls 0: measures nothing

```
